# NICAI Constitutional Runtime — Registry Evidence

## 1. Purpose

This directory contains evidence related to registry participation and registry integration for the NICAI Constitutional Runtime.

The purpose of this evidence is to document:

* registry-related capabilities present in NICAI,
* local registry participation,
* registry adapter boundaries,
* contract preparation,
* trace propagation,
* replay expectations,
* ownership boundaries,
* external registry dependencies,
* evidence status.

This document does **not** invent or assume an external registry service where a canonical external service contract has not been provided.

---

# 2. Registry Evidence Boundary

The NICAI registry boundary is:

```text
NICAI Runtime
      ↓
Registry Adapter / Registry Contract Preparation
      ↓
Bounded Registry Payload
      ↓
External Registry
```

NICAI may prepare registry-compatible information.

The external registry owns its own:

```text
storage
indexing
search
persistence
knowledge management
external lifecycle
external governance
```

NICAI must not claim ownership of those external functions without explicit evidence.

